   "$toggleable_groups": "WHAT MAY BE SWITCHED OFF, and what may not.\n\n`protected` and `access` are NOT toggleable and are ON by default. A national park, an ecological reserve, an Indian reserve and land the public may not enter are all reasons a person can be somewhere they should not be, and none of them is a preference. They were both toggleable and hidden by default, which meant the map's normal state was one that showed none of them.\n\n`ownership` IS toggleable and off by default, and that asymmetry is the point: title is context, not an instruction. It carries private land ONLY — most of British Columbia is Crown land, so drawing that would be a wash over the whole province saying almost nothing. Private title on the bank you meant to walk down is worth looking up deliberately.",
